From: cnjn <1779895255@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] outbound: send a zero address in the SOCKS5 UDP ASSOCIATE

dae 2.1.1 pins olicesx/outbound cc86ced2e683, whose SOCKS5 dialer puts the
first target into DST.ADDR/DST.PORT of the UDP ASSOCIATE request. RFC 1928
section 7 defines that field as the client's own source (zeros when
unknown), and servers that enforce it drop every datagram, so all proxied
UDP through such a node times out.

Pin the same revision plus the one-line fix until it is merged upstream:
https://github.com/cnjn/outbound/commits/dae-2.1.1-socks5-udp-associate
---
--- a/go.mod
+++ b/go.mod
@@ -133,4 +133,4 @@
 // no usable TLS 1.3 key share, rebuilds the ClientHello up to sixteen times
 // while a randomized fingerprint has not produced one, and resolves fingerprint
 // names the way Xray and sing-box do.
-replace github.com/daeuniverse/outbound => github.com/olicesx/outbound v0.0.0-sticky-ip.0.20260918090140-cc86ced2e683
+replace github.com/daeuniverse/outbound => github.com/cnjn/outbound v0.0.0-sticky-ip.0.20261023221000-55000ed9a1c1
--- a/go.sum
+++ b/go.sum
@@ -51,6 +51,8 @@
